+### 2026-10-04 — PROPOSED, awaiting Justin: this repository is reference-only
+
+> **Proposed, not decided.** Written by an entropy-assessment run on 2026-10-04. It becomes a
+> decision only when Justin records it, dated and attributed. Until then it changes no intent
+> document.
+
+**What is unrecorded.** The banners at the top of `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` say this repository is
+reference-only: "Current Personal Agent architecture lives in `../personal-agent`; the current Scope
+and Project model lives in `../../scope`. Do not extend or reinterpret this blueprint as current
+design without explicit authorization." No entry in this log records that change, when it was made,
+or what it still permits. The rest of the repository (AGENTS.md "Session start", ROADMAP.md,
+`skills/session-kickoff.md`, `skills/entropy-guard.md`) still runs it as the live design source.
+
+**Proposed decision** (each part is a recommendation to Justin, not an answer from him):
+
+1. This repository is a reference record of the Sol 0.x blueprint as it stood at the 2026-07-26
+   temporal coordinator entry. It is not current architecture authority.
+2. Changes permitted here: corrections that make the record accurate, each citing the entry that
+   settles it; pointers to the repository that now owns a concept; moves into `archive/`. Any other
+   change needs Justin's recorded authorisation in this file first.
+3. It stays at its current path as a consulted reference, rather than moving to `~/pro-archive/`
+   (see "Local directory structure", 2026-04-04).
+4. The temporal coordinator's contract is owned by the `temporal-coordinator` repository.
+   `components/temporal-coordinator/SPEC.md` and `SCHEDULING.md` are the last blueprint copies.
+5. The open questions below and the ROADMAP.md checkboxes are frozen as historical. Live questions
+   belong in the repositories that now own each concept.
+
+**Would supersede, once decided:** for this repository only, the description of `agentic-architecture`
+as "the bleeding-edge design source for the current named version" in "Five layers clarify
+blueprint, release, installation, runtime, and live state" (2026-04-23).
